Wednesday Update
* Sold half GM, MSFT calls for 30% gain each; buy COST calls* Stocks rip hi=
gher led by value, financials and industrialsStocks are rambling higher mid=
day as benign inflation data last month softened concerns over price pressu=
res and pushed bond yields lower.The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 1.3%=
 to hit a new high, the S&amp;P 500 rose 0.7% and the Nasdaq Composite gain=
ed 0.2%.At current levels, the S&amp;P and the Nasdaq are also sitting clos=
e to record levels struck last month. The Nasdaq staged a sharp recovery on=
 Tuesday following a recent sell-down on an uptick in yields.On Wednesday, =
the US 10-year Treasury yield fell to 1.526% from 1.596% in the previous da=
y after data showing a 0.4% increase in consumer prices for February, compa=
red with January's 0.3% rise."Despite inventory shortages, commodity price =
pressures and supply bottlenecks, inflation continues to be very tame," Jef=
feries economist Aneta Markowska said in a note. "It's likely that business=
es expect these cost pressures to be transitory, and are therefore choosing=
 to absorb them in order to avoid undue price volatility."Meanwhile, Genera=
l Electric (GE) fell more than 6% after striking a deal to sell its GE Avia=
tion Services business to Irish rival AerCap (AER) for over $30 billion to =
focus on its "industrial core" of operations and pay down debt.Tesla (TSLA)=
 gained near 1% after an almost 20% jump on Tuesday. Still, the electric-ca=
r maker was down from its January's record high of $883.09. Other major tec=
h stocks were lower, including Apple (AAPL), Twitter (TWTR), Facebook (FB) =
and Amazon (AMZN).Portfolio: We sold half positions in new GM and MSFT call=
s for 30% gains each today; adjust stops. =E2=80=A6 We now have one new ide=
a for you.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSGeneral Motors (GM) March $50 calls-- Sym=
bol: GM210319C00050000-- Bought at $5.00 on Tuesday, Mar 9 -- Sold half at =
$6.50 today, Mar 10, for a gain of 30%-- Now trading at $6.50-- Set up to s=
ell second half at $8.50 lmt gtc-- Set stop at new $5.20 stp, good after 10=
:30 a.m. ET only*Microsoft Corp.(MSFT) March $232.50 calls-- Symbol: MSFT21=
0319C00232500 -- Bought at $5.00 on Tuesday, Mar 9 -- Sold half at $6.50 to=
day, Mar 10, for a gain of 30%-- Now trading at $4.50-- Set up to sell seco=
nd half at new $8.00 lmt gtc-- Set stop at new $3.90 stp, good after 10:30 =
a.m. ET only*NEW RECOMMENDATIONCostco Wholesale (COST) March 322.50 calls--=
 Symbol: COST210319C00322500-- Order: Buy at $5.50 lmt day only-- If filled=
, set up to sell half at $7.15 lmt gtc and half at $9.35 lmt gtc-- If fille=
d, set stop at $3.85 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET onlyThanks for reading,J=
on D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the th=
ird Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are goo=
d after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are =
good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at t=
he close of the current session. Past results are no guarantee of future re=
turns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendations are=
 leveraged and speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money =
you can afford to lose. All results are shown ex-commissions and fees. Opti=
ons trading involves the risk of substantial loss. Some news and research p=
rovided by Wall Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires a=
nd Reuters.&nbsp;

